  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nFutures are grinding higher despite escalating Middle East tensions, with SPY at $739.30 (+0.23%) and VIX climbing to 28.47. Energy and tech are leading the charge while defensive sectors lag, suggesting traders are betting on war premium rather than safe haven flows.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>CPI Print (12:30 ET)</strong> - Core inflation data will drive Fed expectations and afternoon volatility</li>\n<li><strong>Fed Williams Speech (7:15 ET)</strong> - Any hawkish tilt could pressure risk assets given current VIX levels</li>\n<li><strong>Iran Strait of Hormuz Expansion</strong> - Oil supply disruption fears keeping energy bid, watch crude breakout</li>\n<li><strong>ADP Employment Weekly (12:15 ET)</strong> - Labor market strength gauge ahead of Friday's jobs report</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nEnergy (XLE +2.64%) is the clear winner on Iran escalation, while defensive plays like staples and utilities are getting sold. Tech's 1.34% pop suggests algos are buying growth on any dip, but comm services weakness (-1.16%) shows selective rotation within growth names.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>VIX at 28 creating oversold conditions while indices hold above key support - classic setup for relief rally if CPI comes in soft</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Iran expanding Hormuz definition is major escalation - oil shock could trigger stagflation fears and force Fed's hand</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>12:30 ET CPI release is the real market mover today - everything else is noise until we get that number</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY $735</strong> - Critical support from Friday's low, break triggers 2% selloff</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ $710</strong> - Must hold for tech leadership narrative to stay intact</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 30</strong> - Breakout level that historically signals deeper correction ahead</li>\n<li><strong>XLE $95</strong> - Energy breakout target if oil supply fears intensify</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>"
